Verdict: NEED_MORE
Rationale: The claim states that the Inglis Barracks bombing was the first IRA attack in England since a bombing whose purpose was to kill Prime Minister Margaret Thatcher. While the evidence confirms that the last IRA attack in England before the Inglis Barracks bombing was the 1996 Docklands bombing, it does not establish the purpose of the Docklands bombing as being to kill Margaret Thatcher. The Brighton hotel bombing of 1984, which did aim to kill Thatcher, is not mentioned as the last attack before Inglis Barracks. Therefore, the material part of the claim regarding the purpose of the prior attack remains insufficiently evidenced.
Rounds: 6, findings: 7
